WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.868
-Our first guest tonight is an Emmy-nominated

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.734
and Tony Award-winning actor you know from shows such as

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.567
"Schmigadoon!", "The Good Wife," and "The Good Fight."

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.267
He hosts "The Traitors," which is streaming now on Peacock.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:11.467
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.767
♪♪

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.434
[ Cheering ]

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:20.234
♪♪

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.367
-Welcome to the Highlands of Scotland,

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.133
and welcome to "The Traitor."

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:27.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.501
Stunning, right?

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:29.968
-Yeah. -Yes!

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.267
-And what about the castle?

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:36.968
My most esteemed guests.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:42.767
You are about to enter a world of backstabbing and treachery.

00:00:42.767 --> 00:00:44.701
And you thought "The Real Housewives of Beverly Hills"

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.033
was bad. [ Laughter ]

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:48.501
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.100
our friend Alan Cumming, everybody!

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:57.634
♪♪

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:03.200
♪♪

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.934
It is so good to have you back.

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:06.501
-It's lovely to be here as always.

00:01:06.501 --> 00:01:08.567
-You know, "treachery" is a really good word for you.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.934
-Do you think?

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.200
-Yeah, "treachery" with your accent is just marvelous.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.701
-The treachery, yes.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.701
I just -- It's been such fun because of this show.

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:19.234
There's all these things about how I sound,

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:24.501
how I say "murder" and "quarter of a million dollars."

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:26.801
People are going absolutely nuts for it.

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.667
-You actually -- The way you say "quarter of,"

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.133
it makes it sound better than an actual million dollars.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:32.234
-Yes.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.000
I think it's such a lot of money, though,

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.634
to earn on a little game show. -Yeah.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:37.734
And, now, this is -- You've been on this show

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:39.400
so many times promoting so many different things --

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.000
films, plays, one-man shows --

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.701
and now you're hosting a reality competition show.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.567
Were you excited about this?

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.000
-Uh, I mean, I am excited.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.801
-Yeah. -But it wasn't --

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:52.667
It wasn't, like, in my trajectory that I thought -- -

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.033
-Yeah, it wasn't on your to-do list.

00:01:54.033 --> 00:01:55.501
-No. It just was one of these --

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:58.067
But I think I'm open to -- I obviously come and talk to you

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.834
about lots of weird things I've done.

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.767
Like, the last time, it was a solo dance theater piece.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.200
Let's not forget. -Let's not.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.400
-This is not as crazy as that.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.334
But I just -- They asked me,

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.067
and I couldn't really understand why.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.133
You know, I thought, "I'll take the meeting."

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:14.033
And then I realized they wanted me to play a character.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:15.501
So, I mean, so I am hosting this,

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:18.000
but I'm really sort of an invented character.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.400
Like, I'm called Alan Cumming,

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.367
but I say, "Welcome to my castle."

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:22.634
It's not my castle.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.701
[ Laughter ] I don't have a castle.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:26.601
And I have all these great costumes,

00:02:26.601 --> 00:02:29.767
and I just sort of camp around down these corridors

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.534
saying things like -- Oh, so, what's great is

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.567
when people -- when people say they like the show now,

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.534
I leave little messages for them.

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:38.734
They say, "Oh, Alan, we're watching you."

00:02:38.734 --> 00:02:41.801
I go, "Seth, you have received the most votes

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:44.267
and are banished from the game.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.300
Please come forward to the Circle of Truth."

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:48.667
That's my catch for this.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:50.634
-I'm so glad you finally got your own Circle of Truth.

00:02:50.634 --> 00:02:53.634
You mentioned your clothes. I mean, it is --

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.067
Your sartorial splendor has always been on display.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.834
But this is just -- [ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.133
And, now, this is a show --

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:00.801
I mean, we should get to the premise of the show.

00:03:00.801 --> 00:03:02.901
-I should say the stylist who did all that

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.901
is called Sam Spector, and he's really good at it.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.834
-He did a fantastic, fantastic job.

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.100
You -- So, the show is called "Traitor."

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.834
-Yeah. -And so three of the contestants

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.567
are sort of selected ahead of time to be --

00:03:12.567 --> 00:03:14.000
-Yes, I tap them on the shoulder.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.801
-Okay. Gotcha. -It's like that game "Mafia."

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.634
You know "Mafia"? -Mafia, murder, yeah.

00:03:17.634 --> 00:03:21.000
-It's basically that. They just pinched it.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.968
And so there's three traitors,

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:25.234
and then the other 17 are called "the faithful."

00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:27.701
And then each night -- So, how the day goes is

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.000
that they meet in the morning, have breakfast,

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.400
and during the night,

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.367
one of them's been murdered by the traitors,

00:03:34.367 --> 00:03:37.701
who all meet with cloaks on in a turret.

00:03:37.701 --> 00:03:40.467
-Now, what are turrets for if not that?

00:03:40.467 --> 00:03:43.334
-Exactly. And so they choose who they want to murder.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.133
So that person doesn't appear at breakfast.

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:46.701
So they're all, "Oh," you know?

00:03:46.701 --> 00:03:49.567
And then I appear in some ridiculous costume

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:52.734
and start spouting Shakespeare and tell them to --

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:55.234
Then there's a task that they all have to do together.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.934
They have to work together, you see,

00:03:56.934 --> 00:03:58.467
even though they're ultimately individually.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:00.567
And they do things like get buried alive

00:04:00.567 --> 00:04:02.567
and get, like, you know, maggots thrown on them and things

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:05.501
and jump out of a helicopter into a freezing-cold loch.

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:07.167
A nightmare.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.734
And then they -- And then they come home,

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:10.968
and they're all talking and,

00:04:10.968 --> 00:04:12.067
"Who's the traitor? Who's the traitor?"

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.234
And then there's my favorite bit.

00:04:13.234 --> 00:04:14.434
It's called the Round Table.

00:04:14.434 --> 00:04:16.267
There's a big round table, and they all --

00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:18.067
And I say, you know, "How far would you go

00:04:18.067 --> 00:04:19.968
for a quarter of a million dollars?"

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:21.767
And then, "The table is yours."

00:04:21.767 --> 00:04:24.601
And so they all start bitching about each other...

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:26.801
And then they have to vote someone off.

00:04:26.801 --> 00:04:28.634
And then that's when I say, "You've received the most votes."

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.133
And then somebody gets murdered,

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:34.200
and the whole circle of death happens again.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.067
And then it's a thing that if you get --

00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:38.434
So, if you get to the end and it's just the faithful,

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:39.868
they share all the money.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:42.400
But if there's one faithful left,

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.100
he gets, or she gets, to keep all the money.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.200
-Oh, that's very exciting. -Oh, it's obsessive.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.367
I'm not a game-show sort of person

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:51.701
or a reality sort of person, but I --

00:04:51.701 --> 00:04:53.634
It was my favorite thing I did last year.

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.968
I mean, I did lots of really exciting, challenging,

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:57.534
artistic things.

00:04:57.534 --> 00:04:59.534
I'm like, "No. 'Traitors.'"

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.767
-You mentioned you don't watch a lot of these.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.567
Now, I know the contestants

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:06.267
are a mix of sort of newbies to reality

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:09.133
and some reality stars from other competition shows.

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.467
-Yeah, there's ten each.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:13.601
There's ten real people and then ten reality people.

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:15.400
-Yeah. -But --

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.534
-I think we all know... there's a difference.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:19.601
-Yes.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:21.334
But what I think is hilarious is,

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.367
I think I didn't realize this until I was talking about

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:24.968
doing this press tour --

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:27.901
that reality and porn are very similar

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:31.667
because, like, if you're in one porn film, you're a porn star.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.067
These real people who are in this reality show

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.434
are now reality-show stars.

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:37.367
So you do one reality show, and you're a reality star.

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.567
-There you go.

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:41.367
-So there's a crossover of porn and reality.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:43.400
-Yeah, that's true. -And I'm here for it.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.567
-Yeah, no one, like, does one accidentally.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:48.534
They're like, "I didn't know till it was over," yeah.

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:50.000
I got a lot more to ask you.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.467
We'll be right back with more from Alan Cumming, everybody!

